data_black_phosphorus
# Phase identity: PyRITE crystal catalog entry [black_phosphorus].
# Bundled full-basis P1 CIF used by the declarative material catalog.
# Catalog provenance and assumptions:
# Ambient black phosphorus is orthorhombic Cmce (No. 64; the modern alternate
# setting of Brown and Rundqvist's Cmca notation) with a=3.3136, b=10.478,
# and c=4.3763 A. Brown and Rundqvist (Acta Cryst. 19, 684--685, 1965;
# doi:10.1107/S0365110X65004140) refined P on 8f (0, 0.10168, 0.08056); its
# eight positions are expanded explicitly below. The puckered
# phosphorene layers stack along b, so the catalog models a b-axis-normal slab.
# Limiting checks: V=a*b*c, 8P stoichiometry, and a finite (020) coupling.
# Validation: black-phosphorus-020-structure
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M 'P 1'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number 1
_cell_length_a 3.3136
_cell_length_b 10.478
_cell_length_c 4.3763
_cell_angle_alpha 90.0
_cell_angle_beta 90.0
_cell_angle_gamma 90.0
